---
title: Neapolitan pizza
servings: 6
tags: [italian, pizza]
source: https://github.com/cooklang/cookcli
description: Needs a very hot oven and the dough from the basics folder.
---

Heat the #pizza oven{} to 450–500 °C. Have every topping ready before you start: once the dough is stretched there is no time to chop.

Dust the work surface with @semolina{}. Lift one ball of @pizza dough{6%balls} out of its tray with a #spatula{}, drop it top-side down into a little @flour{}, dust the underside with semolina and turn it back over.

Press from the centre outwards with the fingertips of both hands so that the air moves to the rim, turning the dough a little each time, until a crust has formed all the way round. Lift it onto your knuckles and stretch it gently, turning as you go, to a base of about 25 cm.

Lay the base on a floured surface and spread @tomato sauce{5%tbsp} over it, leaving the rim bare. Scatter over @basil{}(fresh leaves) and tear over the @mozzarella{100%g}.

Flour the #pizza peel{}, slide the pizza onto it, then into the oven. Turn it every few seconds so that it colours evenly; it is done in ~{60-90%seconds}. Slice and eat at once.
